# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# The lab scripts run under bash inside Linux containers. A CRLF checkout on
# Windows (git's default core.autocrlf=true) breaks them: bash reports
# "/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter" or "$'\r': command not found". Forcing LF on
# every text file makes clones correct on every OS, so no one has to strip \r
# by hand after cloning.

# Let git auto-detect text vs binary, and always check out text with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Critical executables / container inputs: always LF (belt and suspenders).
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.php       text eol=lf
*.c         text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.tmpl      text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never apply line-ending conversion.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
